    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d357">

                <pb facs="0455" n="443" xml:id="pg443"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.52/202: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Counselor of Embassy in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-04T19:00:00-05:00">November 4, 1937—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>408. My telegram 407, November 3, 5 p.m. Your telegram no. 817<anchor n="93"
                        xml:id="d357-f1"/> was not received in the Department until 7:45 p.m.
                    November 3. My telegram no. 407 therefore was sent prior to the receipt of your
                    message.</p>
                <p>In the light of the information reported in your 817 I desire to modify somewhat
                    the instructions contained in my 407 regarding your removal to Barcelona. On the
                    understanding that the Minister of State has actually taken up his duties in
                    Barcelona, you are authorized to depart for Barcelona, without further
                    instructions from the Department, simultaneously with or immediately after the
                    departure for that City of your Swedish and Danish colleagues. You will of
                    course bear in mind the desirability of departing for Barcelona before a serious
                    military threat against Valencia develops. Telegraph the Department the date you
                    may fix for departure.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
